<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Own work mode, sitting alongside vanilla's Work / Escort / Recharge /
    Dormant self-charge.

    Why a separate mode instead of changing Recharge:

    Vanilla's Recharge mode deliberately frees the charger again - a mech tops
    up to 100%, steps off and goes dormant beside it, so the next mech in the
    queue gets its turn. That is correct behaviour for a colony with fewer
    chargers than mechs, and we do not want to take it away.

    Docking is the opposite intent: the mech goes to its station and simply
    stays there, awake, holding the spot. That only makes sense when stations
    are assigned per mech, which is exactly what this mod adds.

    Making it a mode rather than a mod setting means the player decides per
    control group instead of globally - some groups can hold their stations
    while others keep cycling through vanilla chargers.

    The work mode picker reads DefDatabase.AllDefsListForReading and sorts by
    uiOrder (verified via decompile), so this appears in the UI automatically
    with no patch. uiOrder 350 places it between Recharge (300) and
    Dormant self-charge (400).

    ignoreGroupChargeLimits mirrors Recharge: the point of the order is "be
    full", so the mechanitor's upper threshold is bypassed and the mech charges
    to 100%.

    SAVE NOTE: a control group stores its work mode as a def reference
    (Scribe_Defs.Look). If this mod is removed while a group is set to Docking,
    RimWorld clears the reference and logs a warning - the group then has no
    work mode until the player picks one again. No data loss, no corruption,
    but worth mentioning in the mod description.
  -->

  <MechWorkModeDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">
    <defName>MS_Docking</defName>
    <label>docking</label>
    <uiOrder>350</uiOrder>
    <description>Go to an assigned mech station, recharge fully and stay there. Unlike recharge, the mechanoid does not step off and go dormant once full - it holds its station until given another order.</description>
    <iconPath>UI/Icons/WorkMode/MS_Docking</iconPath>
    <ignoreGroupChargeLimits>true</ignoreGroupChargeLimits>
  </MechWorkModeDef>

</Defs>
